        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovejoy%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town now houses the remnants of Tara, the fictional plantation from Gone With the Wind, which was moved there in 1979.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovejoy%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lovejoy was incorporated as a town on September 16, 1861, during the early years of the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovejoy%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A cotton gin operated in Lovejoy until 1932, marking the town’s role in the region’s agricultural history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovejoy%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lovejoy sits in southern Clayton County, Georgia, just north of the city of Atlanta.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
